# MEENGLE - DEPLOYMENT GUIDE

## Production Build & Deployment

### Quick Start (Development)

```bash
# Install dependencies
cd backend && npm install
cd ../frontend && npm install

# Start backend
cd backend && npm run dev

# Start frontend (in another terminal)
cd frontend && npm run dev
```

### Docker Deployment (Production)

#### Prerequisites
- Docker & Docker Compose installed
- Environment variables configured

#### Build & Run

```bash
# 1. Create .env file
cat > .env << EOF
JWT_SECRET=your-secret-key-here
STRIPE_KEY=sk_live_your_stripe_key
SENDGRID_API_KEY=your_sendgrid_key
MONGODB_PASSWORD=change_me_in_production
EOF

# 2. Build and start containers
docker-compose up -d

# 3. Verify deployment
curl http://localhost/health  # Frontend health
curl http://localhost:3001/health  # Backend health

# 4. View logs
docker-compose logs -f backend
docker-compose logs -f frontend
```

### Cloud Deployment (AWS, Heroku, DigitalOcean)

#### AWS Elastic Beanstalk

```bash
# 1. Install EB CLI
pip install awsebcli --upgrade --user

# 2. Initialize
eb init -p docker meengle-app

# 3. Deploy
eb create meengle-prod
eb open
```

#### Heroku

```bash
# 1. Login
heroku login

# 2. Create app
heroku create meengle-app
heroku addons:create mongolab:sandbox
heroku config:set JWT_SECRET=your_secret

# 3. Deploy
git push heroku main
```

#### DigitalOcean App Platform

1. Push code to GitHub
2. Connect GitHub repo to DigitalOcean
3. Configure build command: `npm run build`
4. Configure run command: `npm start`

### Continuous Deployment (CI/CD)

#### GitHub Actions

```yaml
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml
name: Deploy to Production

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      
      - name: Build Docker image
        run: docker build -t meengle:latest .
      
      - name: Push to registry
        run: |
          echo ${{ secrets.DOCKER_PASSWORD }} | docker login -u ${{ secrets.DOCKER_USERNAME }} --password-stdin
          docker push meengle:latest
      
      - name: Deploy
        run: |
          ssh ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_USER }}@${{ secrets.DEPLOY_HOST }} \
            'cd /app && docker-compose pull && docker-compose up -d'
```

